There is a knock on the door.
I open the door.
It is my neighbor, Nina.
She has a fresh loaf of bread and a small plant with her.
"For your new home," Nina says.
I am very happy.
I say thank you.
We go into my kitchen.
I put the plant in the window.
I put the bread on the table.
Now the plant stands in the window.
And the bread lies on the table.
"Will you stay and eat with me?" I ask.
"It is my first dinner here."
Nina looks at the small table by the window.
Then she laughs.
"Of course!" she says.
